# TIN TROOP 1-C, start to finish with plain button presses (recorded once
# from a route plan). A stone on the first switch holds its gate open; a
# soldier leaps into the middle of the spikes so the next can use his body
# as a stepping stone; a stone dropped into the shaft weighs down the
# second switch for good. Past the second gate, under a low roof, a pair of
# scales: two soldiers turn to stone on the near pan, so the far pan rises
# and the next soldier rides it up to the hatch in the wall.
